id: pm-context-4gk3
title: "The scalar scanner deletes a same-line reassignment instead of keeping the shell's final value, and persists pipeline and background bindings"
description: "Greptile P1 (security) on PR 84: NPM=ignored; NPM=npm deletes NPM, so a later $NPM publish is omitted from the audit and an attested sibling returns a clean scan over an unattested publish."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: scanner,supply-chain
created_at: "2026-08-31T12:30:22.008Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T12:39:08.354Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T12:39:08.314Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T12:39:08.314Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
resolution: "shellScalars now resolves a same-line reassignment the way the shell does: the last binding that runs in the current shell environment wins (; && and a & ending an earlier background job take the later value); pipeline components, background jobs and command prefixes index nothing; || after an assignment-only left side keeps the earlier value; reassignments whose execution depends on a command's exit status or a compound construct, NAME+= appends, and non-literal values are refused with a delete rather than guessed. The walk is quote-, escape-, backtick- and substitution-aware, and reads 2>&1/>file/&>file as redirections rather than separators."
expected_result: "Eight audit-level regressions each fail against the reverted implementation and pass after: a same-line reassignment keeps the final value the shell would end up with; a redirection on a reassignment is neither a background job nor a pipeline; a pipeline-component assignment is not global provenance evidence; a backgrounded assignment is not global provenance evidence; a command-scoped reassignment leaves the earlier persistent value in place; a reassignment beside a conditional operator follows the shell's own rule; a reassignment inside a compound command is refused rather than guessed; a subshelled or appended reassignment does not carry the earlier value forward."
actual_result: "Revert-proof by hand: restoring the old delete-branch reddened exactly the six tests whose assertions the delete-branch answers (84 pass / 6 fail, every pre-existing test green); reverting the conditional rules to uniform last-wins reddened exactly the conditional-operator test (89/1); removing the compound-command refusal reddened exactly the compound test (89/1). Restored: 357/357 across the suite, npm run coverage 100/100/100, npm run check and npm run release:check green. Note: pm test --run cannot execute this repository's suite inside the linked-test sandbox because PM_PATH is reserved there and the repository's own pm-integration tests (coverage-gaps, context-pack, context-handoff - files untouched by this change) collide with it; every linked command was instead executed directly and observed green, including a single-title run of each recorded test."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T12:30:49.888Z",pi-agent,"Confirmed both halves by measurement before fixing. NPM=ignored; NPM=npm indexed nothing (delete-branch), so audit([npm publish --provenance, NPM=ignored; NPM=npm, $NPM publish]) returned failures: 0 — a clean gate over an unattested publish. The other direction: NPM=npm | cmd and NPM=npm & cmd were BOTH indexed (bash verifies neither persists: pipeline segments and background jobs run in subshells), so audit([npm publish --provenance, FLAG=--provenance | cat, npm publish $FLAG]) also returned failures: 0 — a false pass.\n\nFix: replaced the remainder-check/delete branch with lineScalarBinding, a per-line persistence walk. It splits the line into segments at unquoted ; && || & | (quote-, escape-, backtick- and $()-aware; 2>&1 read as one redirection, not a background job), then keeps the LAST binding that runs in the current shell environment: ; && and a & that ends an earlier background job take the later value; | & and a preceding | index nothing; a command prefix keeps the earlier value; || after an assignment-only left side never runs (assignment always succeeds) so the earlier value stands; a reassignment whose execution depends on a real command's exit status, or that sits in a compound command (then/else/{ }), is refused (opaque, name deleted) because either guess can either attest an unflagged publish or hide an unresolved one; NAME+= and non-literal values refuse the same way. Verified against bash for all 14 persistence shapes (A=1; A=2 -> 2, A=1 && A=2 -> 2, A=1 & A=2 -> 2, A=1 || A=2 -> 1, A=1; A=2 | cat -> 1, A=1; A=2 & bg -> 1, A=1; A=2 cmd -> 1, A=1; (A=2) -> 1, export/multi-assignment/2>&1/> file/&> file/append/compound)."
